      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "body": "Tested ACK 417a548cf23460d87d20ea5d3e1c9c7bcc5af03f\n\nThe new test fails with the one-line fix reverted and passes with it.\n\nI also flipped a signature bit in the final fields of pkh, sh-wpkh, wpkh and taproot key-path inputs, and of the first input of a three-input PSBT whose other inputs were only partially signed. Without the fix, finalizepsbt returned complete=true and a hex whenever the input also had a non_witness_utxo, and testmempoolaccept and generateblock (submit=false) both rejected that hex. With the fix, all of them are complete=false with no hex. Valid, standard signatures give the same result as before.\n\nAs the description says, a final witness that is consensus-valid but non-standard is now complete=false too. I checked with a high-S signature: before, it was extracted when the input had a non_witness_utxo, and now it is not. This matches walletprocesspsbt, so I think it is right, but it may deserve a release note.\n",
